{"term":"second","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:966cea599a6f09ad62","definition":"Number-two; following after the first one with nothing between them. The ordinal number corresponding to the cardinal number two.","example":"He lives on Second Street.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["other"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f63e945d38446eed0f","definition":"Next to the first in value, power, excellence, dignity, or rank; secondary; subordinate; inferior.","example":"His job is second priority, because his family is the most important thing in his life.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["other"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0044d628af57dde154","definition":"Being of the same kind as one that has preceded; another.","example":"Residents of Texas prepared for Hurricane Harvey, which would in some ways turn out to become the second Hurricane Katrina.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["other"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1845b3e46c05ce8dae","definition":"After the first; at the second rank.","example":"Saturn is the second largest planet in the solar system.","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4e0ea1f817eeb8cec0","definition":"After the first occurrence but before the third.","example":"He is batting second today.","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e20708666a50f664ba","definition":"Something that is number two in a series.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f51e9d3ff1010c677","definition":"Something that is next in rank, quality, precedence, position, status, or authority.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:877cb5321b62234f95","definition":"The place that is next below or after first in a race or contest.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7f9eb9e71a90d76958","definition":"A manufactured item that, though still usable, fails to meet quality control standards.","example":"They were discounted because they contained blemishes, nicks or were otherwise factory seconds.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"plural-normally","register":"plural-normally","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d6007c108ffa43de3f","definition":"An additional helping of food.","example":"That was good barbecue. I hope I can get seconds.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"plural-normally","register":"plural-normally","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:03ddb446e64a5302a6","definition":"A chance or attempt to achieve what should have been done the first time, usually indicating success this time around. (See second-guess.)","example":"The policeman smiled, his eyes twinkling. \"Now if you'll follow me, I'll escort you to the Victoria.\"\n\"Oh, there's no need of that. If you'll just point me in the right direction...\"\nThat's what got you in trouble the first time around. You don't need a second.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1bb1e24ddc2103444","definition":"The interval between two adjacent notes in a diatonic scale (either or both of them may be raised or lowered from the basic scale via any type of accidental).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:afaf1bf4ba18cca393","definition":"The second gear of an engine.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2f402e4629e74b9f68","definition":"Second base.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dced5a740c28370a13","definition":"The agent of a party to an honour dispute whose role was to try to resolve the dispute or to make the necessary arrangements for a duel.","example":"Since he [i.e., Abraham Lincoln] had very long arms, he chose cavalry broadswords and took lessons in sword fighting from a West Point graduate; and, on the appointed day, he and [James] Shields met on a sandbar in the Mississippi River, prepared to fight to the death; but, at the last minute, their seconds interrupted and stopped the duel.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e03dba300bff25afb0","definition":"A Cub Scout appointed to assist a sixer.","example":"Many packs have a sixer's council where the sixers, and sometimes the seconds, meet with Akela and some of the other leaders.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["seconder"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cf9b5311ec0b4be034","definition":"A second-class honours degree.","example":"[Stephen Hawking] […] would go to Cambridge, he said, if they gave him a first, and stay at Oxford if they gave him a second. He got a first.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:77bc873ab97f40ae85","definition":"To agree as a second person to (a proposal), usually to reach a necessary quorum of two. (See etymology 3 for translations.)","example":"I second the motion.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second","secondable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:351aeb8d3afd339cb2","definition":"To follow in the next place; to succeed.","example":"In the method of nature, a low valley is immediately seconded with an ambitious hill.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second","secondable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:afde7f4721b8a91c4b","definition":"To climb after a lead climber.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second","secondable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:008d8793c7f466a067","definition":"A unit of time historically and commonly defined as a sixtieth of a minute which the International System of Units more precisely defines as the duration of 9,192,631,770 periods of radiation corresponding to the transition between two hyperfine levels of caesium-133 in a ground state at a temperature of absolute zero and at rest.","example":"Holonyms: decasecond < minute < hectosecond < kilosecond < hour < day < week < megasecond < fortnight < month < year < gigasecond < century < kiloannum, kiloyear, millennium < terasecond < mega-annum, megayear < petasecond < giga-annum, gigayear < exasecond < zettasecond < yottasecond < ronnasecond < quettasecond","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second","secondable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b6dace778e080bf938","definition":"A unit of angle equal to one-sixtieth of a minute of arc or one part in 3600 of a degree.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["arcsecond","second of arc"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosmetic second","diminished second","factory second","major second","minor second","sloppy seconds","this second","secondable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5ecae67976c2538abe","definition":"A short, indeterminate amount of time.","example":"I'll be there in a second.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["instant","jiffy","sec","bat of an eye","bit","blink of an eye","crack","eyeblink","flash","glimpse","half a mo","instant","jiff","jiffy","jot","minute","mo","moment","New York minute","New York second","no time","sec","second","span","split-second","spurt","stound","tick","trice","twink","twinkle","twinkling","while"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":[